WEBVTT

00:08:56.897 --> 00:09:00.444
"Oh," he said. "We solved that problem last week.

00:09:00.444 --> 00:09:02.600
We wrote a compaction routine that reduces

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.180
the size of all fonts by an order of magnitude.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:07.168
You can have as many fonts on your system

00:09:07.168 --> 00:09:08.726
as you like."

00:09:08.726 --> 00:09:11.340
"Well, thank you for letting me know," I said.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.970
Foiled again.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:15.015
I was left with a design solution

00:09:15.015 --> 00:09:19.488
for a nonexistent technical problem.

00:09:19.488 --> 00:09:21.957
But here is where the story sort
of gets interesting for me.

00:09:21.957 --> 00:09:24.552
I didn't just throw my design away

00:09:24.552 --> 00:09:25.953
in a fit of pique.

00:09:25.953 --> 00:09:27.690
I persevered.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.858
What had started as a technical exercise

00:09:29.858 --> 00:09:33.122
became an aesthetic exercise, really.